cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool in security research or operations, please cite the repository and specific commit."
title: "PHP2Shell Fix: PHP Security Assessment and Safe Configuration Mitigation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Felix Studio Developer
repository-code: "https://github.com/felixstudio-dev/apply-correction-PHP2Shell"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/felixstudio-dev/apply-correction-PHP2Shell"
abstract: >-
  PHP2Shell Fix is an open-source Go command-line tool for local PHP CLI
  inventory and version-based security assessment on Windows and Linux.
  It provides read-only native Debian/Ubuntu APT update planning and a
  reversible session upload-progress configuration mitigation for an
  explicitly selected PHP CLI. It does not install PHP security updates,
  verify active web workers, or certify vendor backports.
keywords:
  - PHP
  - PHP2Shell
  - security assessment
  - command-line tool
  - configuration mitigation
  - APT update planning
  - rollback
  - Go
